d_at": "2024-10-31T02:23:54Z", "repo": "Python-pattern-programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b65c05d05e6ae851144a2ca2755a8cff653fa9c9", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2024-10-31T02:23:18Z", "repo": "Python-pattern-programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "f3ab5948b3648b4323a5fedf7708042411f5bc3d", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2024-10-31T02:20:45Z", "repo": "Python-pattern-programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ddd4e4412659146ae34a3a3de2f9aa562818349a", "message": "Create temp", "created_at": "2024-10-31T02:19:52Z", "repo": "Python-pattern-programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "f996dda4508dde65df9bb47d6f473dac8725ca63", "message": "Update and rename leftsidedtri.py to descending_star_triangle.py\n\nThis Python script creates an inverted right triangle pattern using asterisks (*). It has 5 rows, with each row starting with spaces followed by a decreasing number of asterisks. You can change the value of n to make larger or smaller triangles. This example shows how to use nested loops in Python.", "created_at": "2024-10-29T04:55:58Z", "repo": "Python-pattern-programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "1922c309c656d24362b1d750b7ed9a1703c9acc5", "message": "Update and rename increasing.py to right_angled_star_triangle.py\n\nThis program prints a right-angled triangle pattern using asterisks (*). The number of rows is determined by the value of n. Each row contains an increasing number of asterisks, starting from one in the first row to n in the last row. The program demonstrates the use of nested loops to generate patterns, which is a fundamental concept for developing logic and learning control flow in programming.", "created_at": "2024-10-29T04:48:54Z", "repo": "Python-pattern-programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "156fe7ebe73da102ef2fcefa0855d8c23a2bf10f", "message": "Update and rename decreasing.py to inverted_star_triangle.py\n\nThis program generates an inverted right-angled triangle pattern of asterisks (*). The user-defined value n determines the number of rows, and the pattern decreases by one asterisk per row as it progresses. It demonstrates the use of nested loops to create patterns, a common concept in programming for logic building and practice.", "created_at": "2024-10-29T04:45:55Z", "repo": "Python-pattern-programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "f6ede8d1a793ce80edb79d9e2e6f5c5fde8ed35f", "message": "ReadMefile", "created_at": "2024-10-25T00:47:38Z", "repo": "Python-pattern-programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "df4ca170595608beb5b4c02e185ff1144bb8fcb7", "message": "Update README.md\n\nALL STAR PATTERN PROGRAMS IN PYTHON", "created_at": "2024-10-22T23:58:46Z", "repo": "Python-pattern-programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "8b5be77cc18c8d3f8561abb6c71e1b7de67795c1", "message": "Update README.md\n\nAll star/plus pattern programs done in python", "created_at": "2024-10-21T23:46:27Z", "repo": "Python-pattern-programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "e9122adb0870dfe87d4a6a38ba236d433378f9a5", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2024-10-13T02:52:06Z", "repo": "Python-pattern-programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "96b00126b8f1786d7637f5cf4392b0b846b268fa", "message": "Initial commit", "created_at": "2024-10-13T02:48:53Z", "repo": "Python-pattern-programs", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "7ce1d1e9f3d51c3ce8aed77f19850fc2fc832860", "message": "pandas 2D", "created_at": "2025-02-18T00:38:33Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "430bf90a29c2ffa47d54f65816ea6fbe7719df06", "message": "Create Pandas 1D", "created_at": "2025-02-17T10:38:46Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b518ac845658d70eab7b2d88260b8d3a22fef81c", "message": "pandas1", "created_at": "2025-02-16T08:05:16Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "71982817bd50c9860530497b6140a35c48c94de8", "message": "Use of Pandas", "created_at": "2025-02-15T04:22:20Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ae89df922eba898aa8913bd025326821f498ee94", "message": "Update KBCChallenge.py", "created_at": "2024-12-15T07:22:39Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "1b1c74613ccd2a800d1b68c2cca1321400c91223", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2024-11-12T00:08:19Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "e0e3479f62970584534dd85551722cba2b056b66", "message": "Create HTML file", "created_at": "2024-11-12T00:07:39Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "0998e108547f121acedc178f6c9fb134dc762219", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2024-11-04T12:22:52Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "3adda9c18ca8e98cee96ebd6614da0463bc74dc7", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2024-11-03T03:51:18Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ae3996bc6cf4353d65e3080a0bc4ab3c3df50b25", "message": "Update and rename KBC.py to KBCChallenge.py\n\nThis program simulates a simple quiz game inspired by the \"Kaun Banega Crorepati\" (KBC) format. It begins by greeting the user based on the current time of day, using the time module to determine the hour. The user is then prompted to enter their name, followed by three quiz questions. Each question presents multiple-choice options, and the user's answers are evaluated for correctness. If the user selects the correct option, they receive a congratulatory message indicating they have \"won\" a fictional prize; otherwise, they are informed of an incorrect response. This script demonstrates basic control flow, user input handling, and function definitions in Python.", "created_at": "2024-10-26T04:09:51Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "71cb8e816fbd31023fdadc880c6bed7ab6411f35", "message": "Update and rename line plot.py to SimpleLinePlot.py\n\nThis program uses Matplotlib to create a simple line plot. It defines two lists, a and b, representing the x and y coordinates, respectively. The program then plots these coordinates on a graph and displays the resulting line plot. This script demonstrates basic data visualization techniques in Python, showcasing how to create and display a line graph using Matplotlib.", "created_at": "2024-10-26T04:07:26Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "fb0b721f16d1218f55ca8e64474f625f06a33ae4", "message": "Update and rename list.py to PythonListExamples.py\n\nThis program demonstrates various operations involving lists and string membership in Python. It starts by defining a mixed-type list, checking the type of the list, and accessing an element by its index. The program then checks for the presence of specific values within the list and a substring within a string, printing corresponding messages. It also utilizes list comprehensions to generate lists based on conditions: one for even numbers within a range and another for names containing the letter \"o.\" This script showcases fundamental concepts in list manipulation, membership testing, and list comprehensions.", "created_at": "2024-10-26T04:06:25Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b849c70671dcf15790e2e40d41acb531cfaedd42", "message": "Update and rename Image input.py to ResizeAndDisplayImage.py\n\nThis program uses OpenCV to load, resize, and display an image. It begins by loading an image from a specified file path and retrieves its original dimensions (height, width, and channels). The program then resizes the image to a specified dimension of 300x300 pixels, providing feedback on the original and new sizes. Finally, it displays the resized image in a window until a key is pressed, demonstrating basic image processing capabilities with OpenCV in Python.", "created_at": "2024-10-26T04:05:00Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "1a66135c8687be5bd98ec010e616fb342d090e88", "message": "Update and rename prg4.py to StringSlicingAndCounting.py\n\nThis program demonstrates various string manipulation techniques in Python. It begins with a predefined string and prints specific slices, showcasing different ways to access and manipulate string data. The program also counts the total number of characters in the string, stopping when it encounters a period (.). Additionally, it prints each character in the string along with its index, offering insight into string indexing and slicing. This script serves as a simple yet effective introduction to working with strings in Python.", "created_at": "2024-10-26T04:03:39Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ba05c2d44f14ac09d26c4df9e09cae302b61ad6e", "message": "Update and rename prg2.py to NameAccessCheck.py\n\nThis program prompts the user to enter their first and last name to check for access permission. It validates the input against predefined names (\"Vanshraj\" and \"Chauhan\") and provides feedback accordingly. If both names match (case-insensitive), the program grants access with a friendly greeting. If the last name is incorrect, the user is denied access. This simple script demonstrates basic input handling, conditional statements, and user authentication in Python.", "created_at": "2024-10-26T04:02:17Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "684eaf2b650b90772ef7fec420386629382c6937", "message": "Update and rename prg1.py to ComplexNumberOperation.py\n\nThis program performs arithmetic operations involving complex numbers. It prompts the user to input three integers, calculates the result of adding the first two numbers and dividing by the third, and then adds a complex number (78+6j) to the result. The final output displays the computed sum as well as its data type, along with a custom message that incorporates the result. This simple script demonstrates the handling of basic arithmetic and complex number operations in Python.", "created_at": "2024-10-26T04:00:15Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "3f3ced23a30e6b11bb5a5b83521b06722e37752d", "message": "Update and rename mansidi.py to time_waster.py\n\nThis program is a playful and interactive script that starts by asking for the user's name and a 4-digit password, leading to a series of witty and humorous dialogues. It mimics a mock login experience with sarcastic prompts, encouraging the user to stop wasting time and focus on more productive activities. With amusing responses at each step, the program offers a fun way to engage with basic input-output operations in Python.", "created_at": "2024-10-26T03:57:44Z", "repo": "Experiment-Zone", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "72d5d85c3ff0e96d04d7d1799cb1875db5a1e